From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shengyong Zhou <shengyong.zhou@realsenseai.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: tegra: add native DT 0x32 ODPD capture row

Expose an 8-bit GREY surface whose CSI match data type is USER_3
(0x32).  A dedicated media-bus code keeps format discovery scoped to
the ODPD subdevice while reusing the standard GREY V4L2 ABI and RAW8
memory writer.

When a fourcc has multiple format rows, prefer the row enumerated by the
channel's subdevice.  This keeps S_FMT(GREY) on the ODPD-specific mbus row
without adding a product fourcc or an ODPD-name check.

The VI selects the resulting DT match before capture and DMA writes
directly into the ODPD vb2 queue.  No payload copy or post-capture software
demux is added.

Signed-off-by: Shengyong Zhou <shengyong.zhou@realsenseai.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/core.c        | 9 +++++++--
 .../media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/vi5_formats.h     | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/core.c
@@ -153,15 +153,20 @@ tegra_core_get_format_by_code(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 const struct tegra_video_format *
 tegra_core_get_format_by_fourcc(struct tegra_channel *chan, u32 fourcc)
 {
+	const struct tegra_video_format *fallback = NULL;
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < chan->num_video_formats; ++i) {
-		if (chan->video_formats[i]->fourcc == fourcc)
+		if (chan->video_formats[i]->fourcc != fourcc)
+			continue;
+		if (!fallback)
+			fallback = chan->video_formats[i];
+		if (test_bit(i, chan->fmts_bitmap))
 			return chan->video_formats[i];
 	}
 	spec_bar();
 
-	return NULL;
+	return fallback;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(tegra_core_get_format_by_fourcc);
 

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/vi5_formats.h b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/vi5_formats.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/vi5_formats.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/vi5_formats.h
@@ -182,6 +182,9 @@ static const struct tegra_video_format vi5_video_formats[] = {
 	TEGRA_VIDEO_FORMAT_OVERRIDE(RAW8, 8, RS_NV12_FLAT_1X8, 1, 1, T_R8,
 				RAW8, NV12, "NV12 flat over RAW8",
 				0, 0, 1, 1, 3, 2),
+	TEGRA_VIDEO_FORMAT(RAW8, 8, D5X_ODPD_1X8, 1, 1, T_R8,
+				USER_3, GREY, "D5xx ODPD over DT 0x32"),
+
 
 };
 
